# Reject packages published less than 3 days ago (supply-chain defense).
# See: https://github.com/jikig-ai/soleur/issues/1174
#
# This replaces bunfig.toml's `minimumReleaseAge = 259200`, which was expressed in
# SECONDS; npm's key is in DAYS, so 259200s == 3d is the same floor, not a new one.
#
# Load-bearing on the `npm@11` pin in ci.yml's lockfile-sync job: npm 10.x ignores this
# key silently, so a downgrade there would disable the floor with no error.
#
# One file per install directory, and that is not redundancy: npm reads `./.npmrc` from
# the install cwd and does NOT traverse to a parent (measured behaviorally under npm
# 11.12.1 — a parent floor did not apply in a child directory).
#
# The repo ROOT deliberately has no .npmrc. Root-cwd commands include global exact pins
# (`npm install -g likec4@1.50.0`, `@anthropic-ai/claude-code@${CLI_VERSION}`,
# `playwright@1.60.0`), and the floor DOES apply to exact pins: a pin to a version
# published today fails ETARGET under it. That would break the model-launch-review flow
# on the very PR that repins the CLI. See ADR-191.
min-release-age=3
